     "type": "key",
     "style": "definition",
     "title": "Matter",
     "md": "**Matter** is anything that has mass and takes up space. It is made of tiny **particles**. The three **states of matter** are solid, liquid and gas.\n\n- **Solid**: fixed shape and volume; particles packed in a pattern, only vibrating.\n- **Liquid**: fixed volume, takes the shape of its container; particles close but sliding.\n- **Gas**: no fixed shape or volume; particles far apart and moving fast."
