     "md": "A **mixture** has two or more substances that are not chemically joined and can be separated. A **solution** forms when a **solute** dissolves in a **solvent** (salt in water). A **suspension** has solid pieces that stay mixed for a while and then settle (muddy water). Water is a good solvent."
